Auto-acknowledge bundled external extensions on Linux.

package.sh stages the Chromium Web Store extension into
out/Default/extensions as an external-pref CRX, which lands in the
AppImage at opt/aerium/extensions - the directory Chromium resolves
chrome::DIR_EXTERNAL_EXTENSIONS to (DIR_MODULE/extensions), with no
admin-ownership check on Linux.

The extension was still not usable on a fresh launch, because the
provider for that directory never acknowledges what it finds. An
unacknowledged external extension is installed but held disabled
behind an external-install prompt, so the web store simply is not
there. The Windows repo already had to call set_auto_acknowledge for
its own bundled provider; this is the same fix for the Linux path.

--- a/chrome/browser/extensions/external_provider_impl.cc
+++ b/chrome/browser/extensions/external_provider_impl.cc
@@ -855,14 +855,22 @@
     registry_provider->set_allow_updates(true);
     provider_list->push_back(std::move(registry_provider));
 #else
-    provider_list->push_back(std::make_unique<ExternalProviderImpl>(
+    // Aerium: auto-acknowledge this source. The AppImage ships the Chromium
+    // Web Store extension as an external-pref CRX in DIR_EXTERNAL_EXTENSIONS
+    // (DIR_MODULE/extensions), and without acknowledgement an external
+    // extension is installed but left disabled pending an "external install"
+    // prompt, so a fresh AppImage launch shows no web store. Windows already
+    // needed the same treatment for its bundled provider.
+    auto bundled_pref_provider = std::make_unique<ExternalProviderImpl>(
         service,
         base::MakeRefCounted<ExternalPrefLoader>(
             chrome::DIR_EXTERNAL_EXTENSIONS, check_admin_permissions_on_mac,
             nullptr),
         profile, ManifestLocation::kExternalPref,
         ManifestLocation::kExternalPrefDownload,
-        bundled_extension_creation_flags));
+        bundled_extension_creation_flags);
+    bundled_pref_provider->set_auto_acknowledge(true);
+    provider_list->push_back(std::move(bundled_pref_provider));
 
     // Define a per-user source of external extensions.
 #if BUILDFLAG(IS_MAC) || ((BUILDFLAG(IS_LINUX) || BUILDFLAG(IS_CHROMEOS)) && \
